    obligations for the GPL-licensed parts.

Status of the Kokoro replacement (issue #21)
-------------------------------------------
Nox now ships a second text-to-speech engine, Kokoro (`voice.tts.engine: kokoro`, optional
extra `voice-kokoro`). Kokoro's own code, the ONNX Runtime it uses and the `kokoro-v1.0`
model files are permissively licensed. The `kokoro-onnx` package, however, still declares a
hard dependency on `phonemizer` (GPL-3.0-or-later) and `espeakng-loader` (which ships
espeak-ng, GPL-3.0-or-later) for its grapheme-to-phoneme front end.

Selecting Kokoro therefore removes Piper, but it does NOT by itself make a bundled build
Apache-2.0-only: the GPL obligations above apply unchanged to any distribution that includes
the `voice-kokoro` extra. Reaching an Apache-2.0-only installer needs a permissively licensed
grapheme-to-phoneme front end (or a Kokoro front end that accepts phonemes produced by one).
This is an open decision for the project, not a solved problem.

Supertonic 3 text-to-speech (optional `voice-supertonic` extra) - MODEL LICENSE: OpenRAIL-M
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
